    jjFinalCommentEn: "The leaders have almost all the pieces in front of them. ETR sees AI and technology shifts. C, V and M see the skills and jobs problems. L sees the need for a clear map into society. MP and V see belonging. S sees the state's promise. M sees that language and work must be connected. Yet no one assembles the pieces. The most revealing image is ETR's two appearances in the same debate: first AI as shared national infrastructure, an hour later integration without a single AI tool. Politics does not lack puzzle pieces. It lacks the table on which to assemble them.",
